{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant that exposes all sensing and motion events, then encode the exploration policy in a small deterministic specification with clear exploration, short forward progress, and obstacle-recovery commit states. Recovery is conservative after obstacle events, but path_clear returns quickly to exploration. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensing and actuation separately in the plant: one sensor plant for obstacle observations and one motion-capability plant for all commands.",
    "Use one integrated policy specification with exactly one controllable action per active state, random_walk as the default clear-state exploration action, short move_forward only in a dedicated progress state, and directed turn recovery for left/right obstacles plus brief backward escape for front obstacles."
  ],
